{"type":"Binding site","start":167,"end":167,"description":"Ca(2+)"},{"type":"Binding site","start":169,"end":169,"description":"Ca(2+)"},{"type":"Binding site","start":171,"end":171,"description":"Ca(2+)"},{"type":"Binding site","start":176,"end":176,"description":"Ca(2+)"},{"type":"Domain","start":320,"end":464,"description":"PI-PLC X-box"},{"type":"Active site","start":335,"end":335,"description":""},{"type":"Active site","start":380,"end":380,"description":""},{"type":"Domain","start":489,"end":523,"description":"PH 2; first part"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":506,"end":506,"description":"Phosphotyrosine"},{"type":"Domain","start":550,"end":657,"description":"SH2 1"},{"type":"Domain","start":668,"end":756,"description":"SH2 2"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":771,"end":771,"description":"Phosphotyrosine; by SYK"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":775,"end":775,"description":"Phosphotyrosine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":783,"end":783,"description":"Phosphotyrosine; by ITK, SYK and TXK"},{"type":"Domain","start":791,"end":851,"description":"SH3"},{"type":"Domain","start":895,"end":931,"description":"PH 2; second part"},{"type":"Domain","start":953,"end":1070,"description":"PI-PLC Y-box"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":977,"end":977,"description":"Phosphotyrosine"},{"type":"Domain","start":1071,"end":1194,"description":"C2"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":1221,"end":1221,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":1222,"end":1222,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":1227,"end":1227,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":1233,"end":1233,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":1248,"end":1248,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":1253,"end":1253,"description":"Phosphotyrosine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":1263,"end":1263,"description":"Phosphoserine"}],"interfaces":{},"subunit":[{"topic":"Subunit","text":"Interacts with AGAP2 via its SH3 domain. Interacts (via SH2 domain) with RET. Interacts with FLT1 (tyrosine-phosphorylated) (By similarity). Interacts (via SH2 domain) with FGFR1, FGFR2, FGFR3 and FGFR4 (phosphorylated). Interacts with LAT (phosphorylated) upon TCR activation. Interacts (via SH3 domain) with the Pro-rich domain of TNK1. Associates with BLNK, VAV1, GRB2 and NCK1 in a B-cell antigen receptor-dependent fashion. Interacts with CBLB in activated T-cells; which inhibits phosphorylation. Interacts with SHB. Interacts (via SH3 domain) with the Arg/Gly-rich-flanked Pro-rich domains of KHDRBS1/SAM68. This interaction is selectively regulated by arginine methylation of KHDRBS1/SAM68. Interacts with INPP5D/SHIP1, THEMIS and CLNK (By similarity). Interacts with AXL, FLT4 and KIT. Interacts with RALGPS1. Interacts (via the SH2 domains) with VIL1 (phosphorylated at C-terminus tyrosine phosphorylation sites). Interacts (via SH2 domain) with PDGFRA and PDGFRB (tyrosine phosphorylated). Interacts with PIP5K1C (By similarity). Interacts with NTRK1 and NTRK2 (phosphorylated upon ligand-binding). Interacts with SYK; activates PLCG1. Interacts with GRB2, LAT and THEMIS upon TCR activation in thymocytes (By similarity). Interacts with TESPA1; the association is increased with prolonged stimulation of the TCR and may facilitate the assembly of the LAT signalosome. Interacts (via C-terminal proline-rich domain (PRD)) with PLCG1 (via SH3 domain); this interaction leads to guanine nucleotide exchange from PlCG1 to DNM1 and enhances DNM1-dependent endocytosis (By similarity)"},{"topic":"Subunit","text":"(Microbial infection) Interacts (via SH3 domain) with HEV ORF3 protein"}],"isoforms":[{"accession":"P19174-2","name":"2","synonyms":[],"notes":[],"length":1291,"transcripts":{"ensembl":["ENST00000685551.1","ENST00000244007.7"],"refseq":["NM_002660.3"],"refseqProteins":["NP_002651.2"],"maneSelect":true,"decay":[],"onlyDecay":false},"segments":[[1,1,1215],[1217,1216,75]],"edits"